h. Overall, these guidelines serve as a crucial tool in both clinical settings and general health promotion, advocating for proper dietary practices that contribute to overall well-being.", "INFANT FORMULAS:Infant formulas are specialized food products designed to meet the nutritional needs of infants, especially those who are not breastfed.", "NUTRITIONAL EMERGENCY:Nutritional emergency refers to the critical situation where preterm newborns require immediate nutritional support to prevent malnutrition.", "NUTRITIONAL NEEDS:Nutritional needs encompass the dietary requirements essential for maintaining health across various populations. This includes the specific needs of older adults, who require adequate trace elements and vitamins to support their well-being. Additionally, nutritional needs vary significantly for preterm infants, whose dietary requirements differ from those of full-term newborns, necessitating careful consideration and tailored nutrition plans. Furthermore, for patients undergoing nutritional support, particularly in critical care settings, it is crucial to calculate and meet their specific dietary requirements to ensure optimal recovery and health outcomes. Overall, nutritional needs are diverse and must be addressed according to the unique requirements of different groups.", "LECHE MATERNA DONADA:Donated human milk (LMD) is recognized as a second option when maternal milk is unavailable, used under specific medical indications.", "FÓRMULAS DE PREMATUROS:Formulas designed for premature infants to meet their nutritional needs, providing higher calories, proteins, and minerals.", "ALPREM CLINIC 1:A hospital-use formula specifically designed for premature newborns weighing less than 1,800 grams, with higher protein content.", "ESPGHAN 2010:The ESPGHAN 2010 guidelines provide nutritional recommendations for the enteral feeding of premature newborns.", "RECIÉN NACIDOS PRETÉRMINO:\"Recién nacidos pretérmino\" refers to premature newborns who are born 